",
  "README.md": "# my-api

Generated with [create-prodforge](https://github.com/Keyan-dev/create-prodforge).

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d postgres
pnpm db:deploy
pnpm dev
\`\`\`

The server starts on \`http://localhost:3000\`. Check it with \`curl localhost:3000/health\`.

## Scripts

- \`pnpm dev\`: start the server and restart on changes
- \`pnpm build\`: bundle to \`dist/\` with tsdown
- \`pnpm start\`: run the built server
- \`pnpm test\`: run the tests once
- \`pnpm lint\`: lint with ESLint
- \`pnpm format\`: format with Prettier
- \`pnpm typecheck\`: type-check without emitting

## Configuration

Settings come from environment variables, validated at startup in \`src/config/env.ts\`. See \`.env.example\` for the full list. In development they are read from \`.env\`.

## Endpoints

- \`GET /health\`: the process is up (liveness)
- \`GET /ready\`: dependencies are reachable and the server isn't shutting down (readiness)

## Database

Drizzle ORM with PostgreSQL. Tables are defined in \`src/db/schema.ts\`. After changing it, run \`pnpm db:generate\` to write a SQL migration to \`drizzle/\`, then \`pnpm db:migrate\` to apply it. \`pnpm db:deploy\` does the same as \`db:migrate\`; deploys and the compose \`migrate\` service use it.

## Example users module

\`src/modules/users\` is a small CRUD API that shows the database wiring end to end:

- \`GET /users?limit=20&offset=0\`: list users
- \`POST /users\`: create one from \`{ "email", "name" }\`
- \`GET /users/:id\`, \`PATCH /users/:id\`, \`DELETE /users/:id\`

Copy it as a starting point for your own modules. To remove it, delete \`src/modules/users\`, \`tests/users.test.ts\` and the \`usersRouter\` lines in \`src/app.ts\`.

## Docker

\`\`\`bash
docker compose up --build
\`\`\`

The image is a multi-stage build on \`node:alpine\` that runs as the non-root \`node\` user, with a \`HEALTHCHECK\` on \`/health\`. Commit your lockfile first: the build installs from it.

## PM2

For a VM or bare-metal server. Build, then start one worker per CPU in cluster mode:

\`\`\`bash
npm install --global pm2@7.0.4
pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs
\`\`\`
",
  "compose.yaml": "services:
  app:
    build: .
    ports:
      - \${PORT:-3000}:3000
    env_file:
      - path: .env
        required: false
    environment:
      NODE_ENV: production
      PORT: '3000'
      DATABASE_URL: postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/app
    restart: unless-stopped
    depends_on:
      postgres:
        condition: service_healthy
      migrate:
        condition: service_completed_successfully
  migrate:
    build:
      context: .
      target: build
    command:
      - pnpm
      - db:deploy
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/app
    depends_on:
      postgres:
        condition: service_healthy
  postgres:
    image: postgres:18-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_USER: postgres
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: postgres
      POSTGRES_DB: app
    ports:
      - \${POSTGRES_PORT:-5432}:5432
    volumes:
      - postgres-data:/var/lib/postgresql
    healthcheck:
      test:
        - CMD-SHELL
        - pg_isready -U postgres -d app
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 3s
      retries: 10
volumes:
  postgres-data: {}
",
