    "README.md": "# my-api

Generated with [create-prodforge](https://github.com/Keyan-dev/create-prodforge).

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d postgres
pnpm db:deploy
pnpm dev
\`\`\`

The server starts on \`http://localhost:3000\`. Check it with \`curl localhost:3000/health\`.

## Scripts

- \`pnpm dev\`: start the server and restart on changes
- \`pnpm build\`: bundle to \`dist/\` with tsdown
- \`pnpm start\`: run the built server
- \`pnpm test\`: run the tests once
- \`pnpm lint\`: lint with ESLint
- \`pnpm format\`: format with Prettier
- \`pnpm typecheck\`: type-check without emitting

## Configuration

Settings come from environment variables, validated at startup in \`src/config/env.ts\`. See \`.env.example\` for the full list. In development they are read from \`.env\`.

## Endpoints

- \`GET /health\`: the process is up (liveness)
- \`GET /ready\`: dependencies are reachable and the server isn't shutting down (readiness)

## Database

Prisma with PostgreSQL. The schema is \`prisma/schema.prisma\`. After changing it, run \`pnpm db:migrate\` to create and apply a migration (it asks for a name). The client is generated into \`src/generated/prisma\` on install; \`pnpm db:generate\` regenerates it. \`pnpm db:deploy\` applies pending migrations without creating new ones, which is what deploys and the compose \`migrate\` service run.

## Example users module

\`src/modules/users\` is a small CRUD API that shows the database wiring end to end:

- \`GET /users?limit=20&offset=0\`: list users
- \`POST /users\`: create one from \`{ "email", "name" }\`
- \`GET /users/:id\`, \`PATCH /users/:id\`, \`DELETE /users/:id\`

Copy it as a starting point for your own modules. To remove it, delete \`src/modules/users\`, \`tests/users.test.ts\` and the \`usersRouter\` lines in \`src/app.ts\`.

## Docker

\`\`\`bash
docker compose up --build
\`\`\`

The image is a multi-stage build on \`node:alpine\` that runs as the non-root \`node\` user, with a \`HEALTHCHECK\` on \`/health\`. Commit your lockfile first: the build installs from it.

## PM2

For a VM or bare-metal server. Build, then start one worker per CPU in cluster mode:

\`\`\`bash
npm install --global pm2@7.0.4
pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs
\`\`\`
",
    "compose.yaml": "services:
  app:
    build: .
    ports:
      - \${PORT:-3000}:3000
    env_file:
      - path: .env
        required: false
    environment:
      NODE_ENV: production
      PORT: '3000'
      DATABASE_URL: postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/app
    restart: unless-stopped
    depends_on:
      postgres:
        condition: service_healthy
      migrate:
        condition: service_completed_successfully
  migrate:
    build:
      context: .
      target: build
    command:
      - pnpm
      - db:deploy
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/app
    depends_on:
      postgres:
        condition: service_healthy
  postgres:
    image: postgres:18-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_USER: postgres
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: postgres
      POSTGRES_DB: app
    ports:
      - \${POSTGRES_PORT:-5432}:5432
    volumes:
      - postgres-data:/var/lib/postgresql
    healthcheck:
      test:
        - CMD-SHELL
        - pg_isready -U postgres -d app
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 3s
      retries: 10
volumes:
  postgres-data: {}
",
    "ecosystem.config.cjs": "// PM2 process file. On the server: npm install --global pm2@7.0.4
// Build first, then: pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs
// Log rotation: pm2 install pm2-logrotate
module.exports = {
  apps: [
    {
      name: 'my-api',
      script: 'dist/server.js',
      node_args: '--env-file-if-exists=.env',
      // One worker per CPU, sharing the port.
      exec_mode: 'cluster',
      instances: 'max',
      // Each worker calls process.send('ready') once it's listening.
      wait_ready: true,
      listen_timeout: 10_000,
      // Longer than SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS so open requests can finish.
      kill_timeout: 15_000,
      max_memory_restart: '512M',
      env: {
        NODE_ENV: 'production',
      },
    },
  ],
};
",
    "eslint.config.js": "// @ts-check
import js from '@eslint/js';
import prettier from 'eslint-config-prettier';
import globals from 'globals';
import tseslint from 'typescript-eslint';

export default tseslint.config(
  { ignores: ['dist/', 'coverage/'] },
  js.configs.recommended,
  ...tseslint.configs.recommended,
  { languageOptions: { globals: globals.node } },
  {
    rules: {
      // Prefix an unused parameter with _ to keep a required signature, e.g. Express (err, req, res, _next).
      '@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars': [
        'error',
        { argsIgnorePattern: '^_', varsIgnorePattern: '^_', caughtErrorsIgnorePattern: '^_' },
      ],
    },
  },
  prettier,
);
",
